==Finnish==

===Etymology===
From {{der|fi|non|herra}}, from {{der|fi|osx|hērro}}, from {{der|fi|odt|hēriro}}, {{der|fi|goh|hērro}}, the comparative form of {{m|goh|hēr||noble, venerable}} ({{cog|de|hehr}}), by analogy with Latin {{m|la|senior||elder}}. Cognates include Danish, Norwegian and {{cog|sv|herre}}, {{cog|is|herra}}, {{cog|nl|heer}}, {{cog|de|Herr}}. The Old High German word originally meant "grey, grey-haired", and descends from {{der|fi|gem-pro|*hairaz||grey}}, making it cognate with {{cog|ang|hār}} ({{cog|en|hoar}}), {{cog|non|hárr}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|Fi-herra.ogg|Audio|lang=fi}}
